What IS original here
---------------------

- `native/tplconv.cpp` — the on-device weight stage: safetensors reader, the
  quantization rules, and the TPLPACK1 writer.
- `tools/tpl_*.py` — template authoring: the numeric tensor mapping, the rule
  discovery and verification, the pack format and its trimmer.
- The measured results in `README.md`.

These are the parts the MIT licence grants.

SDXL components (2026-09-16)
---------------------------
New SD1.5 and SDXL conversions read CLIP and VAE weights from the selected checkpoint.
The native writer and authoring helpers are original source; their MNN 3.6.1
format references are recorded in tools/clip_recipe.py and docs/CLIP-COMPONENTS.md.
Generated MNN graph recipes, the standard tokenizer, QNN libraries and template
packs remain gitignored. They are not relicensed by the repository's MIT licence.
Checkpoint and upstream component terms still apply.

Legacy backup/restore retains support for the user-published shared ZIP from
https://huggingface.co/Mr-J-369/SDXL-OnDevice-Conversion . It contains MNN text
encoders/embeddings/tokenizer and QAIRT 2.50 v75 QNN VAE encoder/decoder. The VAE
source is identified as madebyollin/sdxl-vae-fp16-fix. These components are not
MIT source and are not bundled in this repository. Generated SDXL template
binaries and packs are also excluded from source control. Neither model family
consumes cached shared weights during new conversions.
